    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Physical and human controls on production",
      "text": "Farm production reflects interactions between the physical environment and human decisions. Relief, climate and soil establish opportunities and constraints, while finance, labour, knowledge, infrastructure and policy affect how those resources are used. A productive explanation follows a connection from factor to farming operation to output. Naming rainfall or capital without showing that connection does not explain a farm's performance.",
