      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Relief is the shape and elevation of the land, including slope. Gentle land can make machinery movement and field layout easier where other conditions are suitable. Steep slopes can increase runoff speed and soil-erosion risk, while making some operations difficult or costly. Terraces or contour practices can alter those relationships, but require appropriate design and maintenance. A steep slope therefore presents constraints that suitable farming practices may address.",
