    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Altitude can influence temperature and growing conditions. It must not be confused with a river or drainage pattern. A map showing close contour spacing gives evidence of steep relief; a river line gives evidence of a watercourse. Both may affect farming but through different mechanisms. A question about relief needs slope or elevation evidence, while a question about water access needs relevant source and supply evidence. Substituting one for the other produces an explanation of the wrong factor.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-1",
