    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Slope aspect can affect exposure to sunshine and moisture conditions. Its importance depends on latitude, season and local setting. Valley bottoms may accumulate deeper material or water, but can also flood or become waterlogged. Upland sites may drain better yet have thinner soil or greater exposure. Use the supplied observations to assess low land’s particular advantages and constraints. The same landform can create a benefit and a hazard under different conditions.",
      "claim_ids": [
