    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Climate includes rainfall, temperature and other long-term weather characteristics. Rainfall amount helps determine whether a crop's water needs can be met, while timing affects germination, growth and harvest. A short intense storm may produce runoff without supplying useful root-zone moisture for the whole season. Long dry intervals can interrupt growth despite a reasonable annual total. Explain the relevant crop stage when possible, rather than treating all rain as equally effective.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-01-1",
