      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Temperature influences growth rate and the length of a suitable growing period. Extreme heat can increase water demand and damage susceptible crops; frost can injure plants adapted to warmer conditions. Requirements differ between crops and varieties. A record of one cold night does not establish the climate, but it can explain a particular frost loss if the crop and exposure are stated. Separate long-term suitability from a short-term weather event affecting one harvest.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-01-2",
