    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Fertility concerns the soil's ability to supply nutrients in forms and amounts plants can use. Repeated removal of crops without adequate replacement can reduce nutrient availability. Soil tests and field observations can help identify a limitation, but a pale crop might also reflect water stress or disease. Choosing a remedy requires evidence about the cause. Fertiliser addresses nutrient supply; it cannot replace missing topsoil or correct every drainage problem.",
      "claim_ids": [
