    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-10",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Soil pH affects the availability of some nutrients, while salts can restrict water uptake. These are different properties. A soil can contain nutrients yet provide poor growing conditions because salinity, compaction or waterlogging interferes with root function. A description such as rich soil is too vague to explain the mechanism. Name the relevant property and its effect on the crop or management operation, using the evidence actually supplied.",
