    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Economic inputs include capital, equipment, purchased materials, transport and access to markets. Capital can finance a borehole, fencing, storage or machinery. Working funds pay for seasonal inputs before sales arrive. A lack of affordable finance may prevent timely planting or repairs even when an investment could increase output. A lender's willingness depends on risk and repayment prospects; approval remains uncertain even where finance is needed.",
      "claim_ids": [
