    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Market access influences what is worthwhile to produce. Perishable vegetables require timely movement and suitable handling. Long journeys, poor roads or unreliable transport can raise costs and losses, reducing the amount reaching consumers. A farm closer to a market may have an advantage, but distance is not the whole explanation: road quality, transport frequency, buyer requirements and competition also matter. Link the specific access condition to saleable output or net income.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-1",
