    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-13",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Incentives influence farmers' decisions. An expected price that covers costs may encourage planting or investment, while uncertain buyers or low returns can discourage it. Policies, contracts or improved information can reduce some uncertainty, but responses depend on available resources. A farmer cannot expand production through price encouragement alone if water, seed or labour is unavailable. Explain how the incentive interacts with the farm's capacity to respond.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-2",
