    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-14",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Social inputs include skills, household labour, education, health, experience and ways of organising work. Knowledge of suitable planting times, soil care or animal management can improve the use of physical resources. Access to extension advice may support new methods where advice is understandable and appropriate. Local experience also matters: a method successful elsewhere may need adaptation to local rainfall, soils and labour. Education is an enabling factor, not an automatic harvest increase.",
      "claim_ids": [
