    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-16",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Political and institutional inputs include land rights, agricultural policy, public investment, security and rules affecting production or trade. Secure and usable access to land can support longer-term investment, while uncertainty or conflict can discourage it. Public roads, water services, research or veterinary programmes can reduce barriers. Whether a stated policy helps depends on delivery, suitability and access; a policy announcement is not the same as farmers receiving a functioning service.",
      "claim_ids": [
