    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-17",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Policies can also create trade-offs. Support for irrigation may increase crop supply while increasing competition for water. A conservation rule may protect a resource but require farmers to adjust practices or bear costs. An evaluation should identify who benefits, who bears costs and over what period. Avoid assuming that a measure has the same effects across producers. Scale, location, water access and market links can influence the distribution of benefits.",
      "claim_ids": [
