    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-18",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Suppose two farms have the same rainfall and crop but different outcomes. A has timely seed, skilled labour and functioning storage; B receives seed late and loses grain through damaged storage. The physical input is similar, while human arrangements affect establishment and usable output. Conversely, similar management may still leave a severe water-supply constraint unresolved. The comparison illustrates interaction, rather than proving that physical or human factors alone determine production.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-2",
