    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-19",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A useful answer selects the factors relevant to its resource. If the evidence shows gentle land, deep soil, a reliable water supply and a poor road, explain each stated advantage or constraint. Do not add a steep slope or an imagined drought. Distinguish observation from inference: an abandoned field is visible, but the cause might require a record of water, labour or market conditions. This evidential discipline connects agricultural explanation with geographical resource interpretation.",
      "claim_ids": [
