      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-21",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Physical interactions can be followed through a short comparison. On a gentle field with deeper soil, more rain may infiltrate and remain available to roots than on a nearby steep, bare, shallow field, depending on soil properties and storm intensity. The second field may lose more water and sediment as runoff. The mechanism combines relief, cover and soil rather than attributing the difference to rainfall alone. A record of equal rainfall helps isolate those other conditions but does not establish that every unmeasured factor is equal.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-1",
