      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-22",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Human interactions are similarly linked. Skills can improve irrigation scheduling, but workers need a functioning system and enough available water to apply that knowledge. Finance can purchase fertiliser, but transport must deliver it in time and soil conditions must permit a response. A better road may reduce costs while a missing store still causes losses. Explain the weakest practical link in the supplied chain instead of assuming that improving one factor solves all constraints.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.08-2",
