      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.08-23",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A decision can also affect people outside the farm. Increased upstream abstraction may limit downstream water under a shared supply; nutrient runoff may affect other users; local hiring may bring income to neighbouring households. These effects connect farm inputs to geographical interdependence. They should be included when the question asks about wider development or sustainability, while a narrowly defined yield question may require only the production mechanism.",
      "claim_ids": [
